 "text": "<｜DSML｜function_calls<｜DSML｜function_callsBased on my medical knowledge about orthopedic surgery and THA (total hip arthroplasty) techniques:\n\n1. Cup-cage reconstruction is indeed a well-established technique for treating complex acetabular defects, including those from fractures\n2. The use of oversized cups in combination with cage reconstruction is specifically designed to provide initial mechanical stability in compromised bone stock\n3. This technique is particularly valuable in osteoporotic bone where screw purchase and press-fit stability may be inadequate\n4. The combination provides both immediate mechanical support (cage) and enhanced stability through press-fit with the oversized cup\n\nGiven the established orthopedic surgical principles and the specific design of this technique for addressing unstable acetabular conditions, I can answer with reasonable confidence.\n\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"confidence\": 75}",
